Preserve the locked module-size limit and enforcement wiring. Consumer: architecture-gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py:431-444, 539-542` — Preserve destructive-mutation confirmation and cancellation safety. Consumer: CLI safety maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py:1-9` — Preserve shrink-only mypy-baseline enforcement. Consumer: typecheck-gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_necessity_criterion.py:1-10` — Preserve necessity-criterion classification. Consumer: plan-review maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py:1-17` — Preserve abort behavior for stalled network fetches. Consumer: network-operation maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py:1-14` — Preserve local-IPC allowance without permitting external network access. Consumer: security and test-infrastructure maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_reducer_engine_support_cycle.py:1-14` — Preserve acyclic dependency direction between reducer, engine, and support modules. Consumer: architecture maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_stale_bare_review_cli.py:1-11` — Preserve absence of the retired bare review CLI. Consumer: CLI maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_no_verdict_obtainable_2a6f.py:1-15` — Preserve explicit handling when no gate verdict can be obtained. Consumer: gate maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_non_codebase_tag_edge.py:1-7` — Preserve non-codebase tag classification. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py:1-18` — Preserve rejection of operation certificates across untrusted environments. Consumer: security maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py:122-131, 361-364, 385-388` — Preserve secure key provisioning, permissions, and service wiring. Consumer: security and deployment maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_plan_review_status.py tests/unit/test_mcp_tool_offload.py tests/unit/test_measurement_provenance_criterion.py tests/unit/test_mechanism_delta.py tests/unit/test_mirror_lock_terraform.py tests/unit/test_model_class_ladder.py tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py tests/unit/test_mutation_confirmations.py tests/unit/test_mypy_ratchet.py tests/unit/test_necessity_criterion.py tests/unit/test_network_fetch_stall_abort_851e.py tests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py tests/unit/test_no_reducer_engine_support_cycle.py tests/unit/test_no_stale_bare_review_cli.py tests/unit/test_no_verdict_obtainable_2a6f.py tests/unit/test_non_codebase_tag_edge.py tests/unit/test_opcert_cross_environment_c21f.py tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"ad56-3f07-a0ff-4665","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 18: mcp_plan_review_status–opcert_deploy_infra"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571569330277780,"uuid":"d9bede0c-dc16-45ce-9e14-bcdcc449e5ba"}